# Form invalid state

Controls that take a value must accept `aria-invalid` and show error chrome. That includes Input, Textarea, Checkbox, Switch, Slider, RadioGroup, Select, and InputGroup fields. Display-only pieces (Card, Badge, Skeleton, Progress) do not.

- Style with a destructive border and ring, matching Input.
- Put `aria-invalid` on the control. For RadioGroup, put it on the group. For InputGroup, put it on the field.
- Include an `Invalid` story. Keep `docs.source.code` in sync, with `useState` and `aria-invalid`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — no invalid styles, or no Invalid story
<Switch checked={checked} onCheckedChange={setChecked} />

// ✅ GOOD
<Switch checked={checked} onCheckedChange={setChecked} aria-invalid />
```
